FerrionOS change to upstream base (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 20f7573b4dc011ea5267189185edc0b2f12bab0f with the patches before it in the recipe's list applied.

NvmeCmdQueue::is_full checked self.head == self.tail + 1 without wrapping modulo the 64-entry queue length, so a 128-command burst from driver-block starting at head 0 wrapped tail past head, overwrote in-flight SQ entries and executor::awaiting_completion tasks, and rang the doorbell with tail == head == 0, stranding RedoxFS in futex wait while nvmed slept on its event queue. Command IDs were also taken from sq.tail and could be reused after fetch before asynchronous completion. Fix is_full with the wraparound mask, allocate command IDs from a bounded 64-bit free mask released only after completion, reject out-of-range sq_head or unallocated cid completions with an error log, and assert no duplicate insertion into awaiting_completion.

